<Addin>
  <!--
    Tells VS4Mac's MEF container to scan this addin's own assembly for
    [Export] components: specifically MdixLanguageClient (implements
    ILanguageClient) and MdixContentDefinition's exports, both in
    MdixLanguageClient.cs. Without this, the host's Mono.Addins loader picks
    the assembly up fine, but MEF composition (a separate mechanism layered
    on top, not something Mono.Addins does for you automatically) never
    finds those exports, so ILanguageClient never activates for .mdix files
    even though the addin itself loads without error.

    File name matches AssemblyName in MdixAddin.csproj, namely "MdixLanguageSupport" —
    not the class name "MdixLanguageClient" or the project name "MdixAddin".

    Source: Matt Ward's own VS4Mac LSP walkthrough (lastexitcode.com,
    "Language Server Protocol support in Visual Studio for Mac 7.4"),
    "Enabling Managed Extensibility Framework Support" section.
  -->
  <Extension path="/MonoDevelop/Ide/Composition">
    <Assembly file="MdixLanguageSupport.dll" />
  </Extension>

  <!--
    2026-08-06 — icon="md-mdix-file" removed. The crash report from this
    build (Issues.txt) shows a real native NSException, thrown mid-redraw
    (Core Animation transaction flush), caught by VS4Mac's own
    VisualStudioApplicationMonitor.CrashOnException — which deliberately
    FailFasts rather than continue with Cocoa's internal state possibly
    corrupted. This build is the first one where the StockIcons extension
    point path was actually correct, meaning it's the first time VS4Mac
    ever genuinely tried to rasterize Resources/mdix-file.svg. The OS field
    in the crash dump confirms 10.15.7  Catalina is literally the first
    macOS version with any native SVG image support (CoreSVG), which makes
    a loose-file (non-Asset-Catalog) SVG load a real candidate for hitting
    an immature/edge-case path in that framework.
    Pulling the icon out entirely for now rather than guessing at the SVG
    again  clean isolation test: if the crash and the folder-expand issue
    both go away without it, that confirms the icon load as the cause, and
    it can go back on the backlog as a cosmetic-only, non-blocking fix. If
    they DON'T go away, we've ruled the icon out completely and know to
    look elsewhere next, rather than re-guessing a fourth time.
    The StockIcons extension block and the two ImportAddinFile("Resources/
    ...") lines in AddinInfo.cs are removed together with this.
  -->
  <Extension path="/MonoDevelop/Core/MimeTypes">
    <MimeType
        id="text/x-mdix"
        _description="DixScript Configuration File"
        isText="true">
      <File pattern="*.mdix" />
    </MimeType>
  </Extension>

  <Extension path="/MonoDevelop/Ide/FileFilters">
    <FileFilter id="Mdix" _label="DixScript Files" extensions="*.mdix" />
  </Extension>
</Addin>
